  "label": "2021-05",
  "text": "In May 2021 we returned, most of us, to a single phrase: nine of us said \"back to work\" by the twelfth. Then the record narrows to law enforcement. Seven of us reached for \"law enforcement officers\" on the thirteenth, the same day seven marked \"national police week\" and seven more said \"men and women who.\" Six of us said \"our law enforcement,\" six \"of law enforcement,\" six \"on the house floor.\" Seven of us named \"world war ii\" late in the month, on the twenty-eighth. That is the shape of us this era: a small chorus, peaking at nine, clustered on one day around the police, and otherwise thin. We coordinated most where we said we honor, and we counted ourselves in single digits.",
